2	// `node worker.mjs` (cwd = this task dir, bounded by code_work_timeout).
3	// The whole task: no agent phase.
4	//
5	// It holds NO counting logic. The counting and folding are `fold-usage.mjs`, its
6	// SIBLING in this task folder — nothing outside this task uses them, so that is
7	// where they live and where their tests point. This file is the I/O shell:
8	//
9	//   1. fetch the orphan `conversation-logs` branch (plain local git — the branch is
10	//      in this repo, so one tree read plus one blob read per file beats any REST
11	//      round-trip, and there is no rate budget to spend);
12	//   2. count each capture file still in the raw retention window;
13	//   3. list the scheduler's and executor's completed workflow runs past the
14	//      `runsFoldedThrough` watermark (read-runs.mjs) — how often the machinery ran,
15	//      including the runs that opened no session at all;
16	//   4. list the work items that CLOSED past the `queueFoldedThrough` watermark
17	//      (read-queue.mjs) — what each occurrence came to, and the parks each collected;
18	//   4b. list the pull requests MERGED past the `prsFoldedThrough` watermark
19	//      (read-prs.mjs) — what each one took from opening, from its issue and from the
20	//      session that did the work;
21	//   5. read the local git history and the releases listing for the day series neither
22	//      of the above can answer — commits, lines and releases;
23	//   6. fold: hour rows over the last three days, day rows recomputed from scratch,
24	//      appended rows past their watermarks, week rows advanced past `foldedThrough`
25	//      (skill-usage-metrics DESIGN §5);
26	//   7. deliver the regenerated `.claudinite/local/usage.GENERATED.json` on a PR
27	//      that lands itself where this repo's delivery settings allow (the shared
28	//      landing helper owns those nuances — packs/claudinite-tasks/land-pr.mjs) — and
29	//      open NOTHING when the recompute is byte-identical apart from its stamp.
30	//
31	// The aggregate lives under `.claudinite/local/` because that is the repo-owned area
32	// the vendoring refresh never touches; the mount root itself is read-only canon.
